      "writtenOn": "2022-12-08T06:15:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Consider making this return a boolean indicating whether or not the network request was successfully submitted. The caller, in this case `loadRebootEscrowDataOnInternet()`, is essentially relying on the callback being invoked to kick off the RoR attempt.\n\nCurrently, if the connectivityManager is null, this function will return and the RoR will not be attempted because there is no callback. Having a return value of false when the ConnectivityManager could not be obtained allows the caller to gracefully handle this by falling back to attempting the RoR without waiting for a network-available callback.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 292,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 292,
        "endChar": 19
      },
