      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see what you mean. Initially, I thought it makes sense that the execution is suspended when the wakelock is no longer held since it\u0027s past the timeout and RoR wouldn\u0027t be guaranteed to finish. But, I can see how this might be confusing from a debugging perspective. \n\nI think just having a wake lock timeout be the original timeout with the extension value you suggested should suffice.",
